		(uuid "b8771598-f94e-40a8-9a43-0a12cf434b7d")
	)
	(text_box "> The SBU1 and SBU2 pins on a USB-C connector are Sideband Use (SBU) pins. They are part of the USB-C standard and serve specialized roles depending on the application, primarily in Alternate Modes (e.g., DisplayPort, Thunderbolt) and certain USB-C accessories.\n> For basic USB 2.0/3.0 operation (like in your ESP32-C3-02 design), the SBU pins are not used and can be left unconnected or handled with optional protective measures."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 60.96 68.58 0)
		(size 64.77 19.0499)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
